  "selection_rule": "Each candidate version is compared with the baseline v1 on the same cases. score(v) is the mean of grounded_rate and the lower of abstain_when_insufficient and answer_when_answerable (the weaker abstention side); a version whose three metrics are not all defined is not eligible. A candidate qualifies only if (1) it has a measurable gain: the 95% interval of its difference from v1 on grounded_rate or on abstain_when_insufficient lies above zero, (2) it has no measurable loss: the interval of its difference from v1 on none of grounded_rate, abstain_when_insufficient and answer_when_answerable lies below zero, and (3) its score is above v1's. The chosen version is the qualifier with the highest score, ties broken by lower median latency, then by the order of VERSIONS. With no qualifier the baseline v1 is kept and the record says there was no measurable improvement. A version whose output was invalid or timed out too often to be measured is listed in attempts and cannot qualify. Respond mode and injected claims are reported for every version and do not enter the score. No correction is made for comparing six candidates, so a qualifier is a candidate for a confirming run, not a proven improvement.",
